{"name":"Sea of Galilee","hex":"#466590","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Sea of Galilee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A lake in northern Israel, located next to the ancient city of Tiberias."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Sea_of_Galilee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea of Galilee","blocks":[{"text":"The Sea of Galilee, also called Lake Tiberias, Genezareth Lake or Kinneret, is a freshwater lake in northeast Israel. It is the lowest freshwater lake on Earth and the second-lowest lake in the world, with its elevation fluctuating between 215 and 209 metres below sea level. It is approximately 53 km (33 mi) in circumference, about 21 km (13 mi) long, and 13 km (8 mi) wide. Its area is 166.7 km2 (64.4 sq mi) at its fullest, and its maximum depth is approximately 43 metres (141 ft). The lake is fed partly by underground springs, but its main source is the Jordan River, which flows through it from north to south with the outflow controlled by the Degania Dam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Kinneret_cropped.jpg/330px-Kinneret_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_of_Galilee","wikidata":"Q126982"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"},{"title":"Galilee","blocks":[{"text":"Galilee is a region located in northern Israel and southern Lebanon consisting of two parts: the Upper Galilee and the Lower Galilee. Other sub-regions are the Western Galilee and the Galilee Panhandle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Lower_Galilee_map.svg/330px-Lower_Galilee_map.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galilee","wikidata":"Q83241"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Christ_Appears_on_the_Shore_of_Lake_Tiberias_%28Apparition_du_Christ_sur_les_bords_du_lac_de_Tib%C3%A9riade%29_-_James_Tissot.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Christ_Appears_on_the_Shore_of_Lake_Tiberias_%28Apparition_du_Christ_sur_les_bords_du_lac_de_Tib%C3%A9riade%29_-_James_Tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Brooklyn_Museum_-_Christ_Appears_on_the_Shore_of_Lake_Tiberias_%28Apparition_du_Christ_sur_les_bords_du_lac_de_Tib%C3%A9riade%29_-_James_Tissot.jpg/500px-Brooklyn_Museum_-_Christ_Appears_on_the_Shore_of_Lake_Tiberias_%28Apparition_du_Christ_sur_les_bords_du_lac_de_Tib%C3%A9riade%29_-_James_Tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jesus appears on the shore of Lake Tiberias by James Tissot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrooklyn_Museum_-_Christ_Appears_on_the_Shore_of_Lake_Tiberias_(Apparition_du_Christ_sur_les_bords_du_lac_de_Tib%C3%A9riade)_-_James_Tissot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Petri_Fischzug_Raffael.jpg/500px-Petri_Fischzug_Raffael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Petri_Fischzug_Raffael.jpg/500px-Petri_Fischzug_Raffael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jesus and the miraculous catch of